BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:barr-trail-mountain-race-2027@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20261115T000000Z
DTSTART:20270718T080000Z
DTEND:20270718T120000Z
SUMMARY:Barr Trail Mountain Race
DESCRIPTION:The Barr Trail Mountain Race is a 12.6 mile trail run up Pikes Peak to Barr Camp and back to the trailhead\, with a maximum elevation of 10\,200 feet. This race serves as the second component of the Garden to Peak Challenge series and provides runners an opportunity to test their training for the Pikes Peak Ascent or Marathon.
LOCATION:441 Manitou Ave\, Suite 100\, Manitou Springs\, CO 80829
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pikes-peak-ultra-2027@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20261115T000000Z
DTSTART:20270724T053000Z
DTEND:20270724T093000Z
SUMMARY:Pikes Peak Ultra
DESCRIPTION:Pikes Peak Ultra is an ultramarathon event featuring multiple distance options (20K\, 30K\, 50K\, and 50 Mile) starting at Bear Creek Regional Park in Colorado Springs. The course winds through stunning trails including High Drive\, Cheyenne Canon\, Seven Bridges Trail\, and Pipeline Trail\, with much of the course on crushed granite. The 50K and 50 Mile options include a summit of Mt. Rosa with panoramic city views. All runners receive a custom race shirt\, BOCO trucker hat\, and finishers' medal.
LOCATION:Bear Creek Regional Park\, 21st and Argus Blvd\, Colorado Springs\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aspen-backcountry-2027@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20261115T000000Z
DTSTART:20270731T060000Z
DTEND:20270731T100000Z
SUMMARY:Aspen Backcountry
DESCRIPTION:Aspen Backcountry offers three race distances (50K\, Marathon\, and Heavy Half-Marathon) run almost exclusively on dirt trails in the beautiful Aspen area. The race features diverse terrain with challenging ascents and descents\, spectacular views of the Elk Mountains\, and will be hosted on the same day as the Duck Derby festival with live music\, food trucks\, and family-friendly activities at Rio Grande Park.
LOCATION:Rio Grande Park\, Rio Grande Parking\, Aspen\, CO 81611
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:leadville-trail-100-mtb-2027@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20261115T000000Z
DTSTART:20270814T060000Z
DTEND:20270814T100000Z
SUMMARY:Leadville Trail 100 MTB
DESCRIPTION:The Life Time Leadville Trail 100 MTB is one of the most prestigious endurance cross-country mountain bike events in the world. Riders tackle a grueling 100-mile course with approximately 12\,000 feet of elevation gain\, starting at 10\,152 feet and reaching a peak elevation of 12\,500 feet at Columbine Mine. The race features steep climbs\, technical descents\, and stunning Rocky Mountain scenery. Finishers can earn the coveted silver or gold beltbuckle with a 12-hour time limit.
LOCATION:135 E 6th Street\, Leadville\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:leadville-trail-100-run-2027@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20261115T000000Z
DTSTART:20270821T040000Z
DTEND:20270821T080000Z
SUMMARY:Leadville Trail 100 Run
DESCRIPTION:The Life Time Leadville Trail 100 RUN presented by La Sportiva is one of the oldest and most storied endurance running events in the world. This brutal out-and-back ultramarathon covers 100 miles of high-altitude\, extreme Rocky Mountain terrain starting at 10\,200 feet. The course includes steep climbs of Powerline\, high-altitude passes like Sugarloaf\, technical terrain on the Colorado Trail\, and two climbs on Hope Pass (12\,500 feet). The race is limited to a select handful of gritty runners via lottery entry.
LOCATION:Corner of 6th St & Harrison\, Leadville\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
